<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pervez Musharraf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a>–<a href="/years/2023">2023</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pervez Musharraf was a Pakistani army general who seized power in a coup in October 1999 and ruled until 2008, as chief executive and from 2001 as president. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> an ally of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> after the attacks of 11 September 2001 and survived several assassination attempts. Faced with impeachment, he resigned in 2008 and later lived in exile in Dubai.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pervez-musharraf.jpg" alt="Pervez Musharraf" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antônio Cruz/ABr · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pervez_Musharraf_2004_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
